      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Lift compatible requirements using nested closed generator sets in compact I. For each σ, a second intersection in the closure of ⟨γ⟩ matches its finite images. The quotient element lies in P by comparing every valuation with a factorial root of p.",
      "review": "Verified the nested kernel argument, both compact intersections and the use of the number-field hypothesis in the final wild criterion."
    },
    {
      "id": "TIC-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Evaluation determines a continuous ℓ-primary character, with ℓ choices for coefficients in the prime field",
      "anchor": "inputs-tame-inertia-detection",
      "statement": "For p≠ℓ and a discrete ℓ-primary abelian group A, evaluation at the chosen tame lift injects Hom_cont(I,A) into A. The finite-field specialization gives at most ℓ possibilities per orbit representative. With A=ℚ_ℓ/ℤ_ℓ each character has finite image and those killed by ℓ^r have at most ℓ^r possible evaluations.",
      "hypotheses": "The coefficient action is trivial and the characters are additive homomorphisms. Inertia is compact and the characters are locally constant. The factor ℓ in CharStep uses 𝔽_ℓ coefficients. The extension to a general primary group follows from the argument and does not change that consumer.",
      "definitions": [
        "I is the absolute inertia group at the chosen prolongation. An open kernel contains its intersection with some fixing subgroup of a finite extension.",
        "For a wild τ and p∤k, τ^k x=x implies τx=x by a telescoping sum on the orbit differences."
      ],
