      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "For σ∈P choose N=ℓ^a b such that σ^N fixes the finite extension cut out by a neighbourhood of the identity, with ℓ∤b. The valuation lemma removes ℓ^a from this power. Thus b annihilates the image of σ, forcing that image to be zero. The closed kernel contains P and γ when the chosen evaluation vanishes. The order-20 finite inertia example gives the counts two and four.",
      "review": "A second reader verified the cyclotomic extension, wild kernel, lift of order four, and the distinct counts for the two discrete targets. All finite-model characters were also enumerated."
